Q: Does Kadane&#39;s Algorithm work when all elements are negative? A: <p>Yes, the answer of <code>0</code> is <em>correct</em> and expected one: when all items are negative the subarray with maximum sum is an <em>empty</em> subarray <code>[]</code>.</p>
<p>If you insist on <em>not empty</em> subarray, you can easily modify the original algorithm:</p>
<pre><code>public static void KadaneAlgoNonEmpty(int arr[]) {
  // Original algorithm here
  ...

  // If Max_Sum == 0 we don't have positive items and we should
  // return the largest item - a subarray of length 1 
  if (Max_Sum == 0)
    Max_Sum = Arrays.stream(arr).max().getAsInt();

  System.out.println(&quot;Max Sum is &quot; + Max_Sum);
}
</code></pre>
